  bootwright / cluster
      Manage cluster

  Usage
    bootwright cluster [flags]

  Commands
  ○ Command | exec
      PURPOSE  Run a command over SSH on cluster nodes' Machines as the Machine's resolved
               identity; confirm or refuse an unproved host key and return the client's exit
               status

  ○ Command | info
      PURPOSE  Show cluster details and static access applicability

  ○ Command | kubeconfig
      PURPOSE  Export raw sensitive kubeconfig bytes to standard output

  ○ Command | kubectl
      PURPOSE  Print a kubectl access descriptor for independent operator execution; do not
               launch a client or connect (unavailable)

  ○ Command | list
      PURPOSE  List container and storage clusters

  ○ Command | oc
      PURPOSE  Print an oc access descriptor for independent operator execution; do not launch
               a client or connect (unavailable)

  ○ Command | rsh
      PURPOSE  Open an SSH session on a cluster node's Machine as the Machine's resolved
               identity; confirm or refuse an unproved host key and return the client's exit
               status

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  More detail
    Use --help --detail full to include SSH overrides.
